hadiths[65]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3021","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three things upon which I swear: Allah Almighty will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share, and the shares of Islam are three: prayer, fasting and zakah. When Allah takes a servant under His care in this world, He will not hand him over to anyone else on the Day of Resurrection. No man loves a people except that Allah will join him with them. And a fourth, which, if I were to swear upon it, I hope I would not be sinning: when Allah conceals the faults of a servant in this world, He will also conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection."
"3022","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I fear three things for my Ummah: attributing rain to the stars, the injustice of the ruler, and denying divine decree."
"3023","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things, when they appear, faith will not benefit anyone who had not believed before or had not earned good through his faith: the rising of the sun from the west, the Dajjal, and the Beast of the Earth (Dabbat al-Ard)."
"3024","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three things upon which I swear: no servant's wealth is diminished by charity; no servant is patient in the face of an injustice except that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, increases him in honour; and no servant opens the door of begging except that Allah opens upon him the door of poverty. And I will tell you something, so remember it: this world is only for four kinds of people. One is a servant whom Allah has blessed with both wealth and knowledge, so he fears his Lord in it, maintains ties of kinship, and fulfils the right of Allah; he is at the best of ranks. The second is a servant whom Allah has given knowledge but not wealth, and, being sincere in his intention, he says: 'If I had wealth, I would do as so-and-so does.' So by virtue of his intention, he receives a reward equal to the first. The third is a servant whom Allah has given wealth but not knowledge, so he acts as he pleases with his wealth without knowledge; he neither fears his Lord in it, nor maintains ties of kinship, nor fulfils the right of Allah; he is at the worst of ranks. The fourth is a servant whom Allah has given neither wealth nor knowledge, and he says: 'If I had wealth, I would do as so-and-so does.' So by virtue of his intention, he is equal to him in sin."
"3025","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three things upon which I swear: wealth is never diminished by charity, so give charity; no man forgives an injustice except that Allah Almighty increases him in honour because of it, so forgive, and Allah will give you honour; and no man opens upon himself the door of begging from people except that Allah opens upon him the door of poverty."
"3026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three things: if there is a cure in anything, it is in cupping, or drinking honey, or cauterisation that reaches the pain, but I dislike cauterisation and do not like it."
"3027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three things in which seriousness is serious and jest is also counted as serious: marriage, divorce and taking back (a divorced wife)."
"3028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are an obligatory right upon every Muslim: taking a ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, using the miswak, and applying perfume."
"3029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three signs of a Muslim man's happiness in this world: a righteous neighbour, a spacious home, and a comfortable mount."
"3030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three supplications are answered: the supplication of the fasting person, the supplication of the oppressed, and the supplication of the traveller."
"3031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three supplications are answered without doubt: the supplication of a father against his child, the supplication of the traveller, and the supplication of the oppressed."
"3032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three supplications are not rejected: the supplication of a father for his child, the supplication of the fasting person, and the supplication of the traveller."
"3033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three supplications are answered without doubt: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveller, and the supplication of a father for his child."
"3034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In three things there is a cure for every disease except death: senna and sanut."
"3035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are a right upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending the funeral, and saying Yarhamuk Allah (May Allah have mercy on you) to one who sneezes when he says Alhamdulillah."
"3036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The emigrant (Muhajir) is permitted to stay three days after the return."
"3037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things will always remain in my Ummah: boasting about lineage, wailing over the dead, and attributing rain to the stars."
"3038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are among the manners of prophethood: hastening to break the fast, delaying the pre-dawn meal (suhur), and placing the right hand over the left in prayer."
"3039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things bring salvation: fear of Allah Almighty in private and in public, being just in contentment and in anger, and moderation in poverty and in affluence. And three things bring destruction: following one's desires, obeying greed, and a man's admiration of himself."
"3040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three practices of the Days of Ignorance which the people of Islam will not abandon: attributing rain to the stars, slandering lineage, and wailing over the dead."
"3041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three deeds, whoever does them will taste the flavour of faith: whoever worships Allah alone and believes that La ilaha illallah (there is no true god except Allah); and pays the zakah on his wealth willingly and regularly every year, giving neither an old animal, nor a mangy one, nor a sick one, nor inferior livestock, but rather from his average wealth, for Allah has not asked you for the best of your wealth, nor has He commanded you to give the worst of it; and purifies his soul."
"3042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days of every month, and from Ramadan to Ramadan: this is as though fasting the whole year."
"3043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has three traits is a hypocrite, even if he fasts, prays, performs Hajj and Umrah, and says, 'I am a Muslim': when he speaks he lies, when he makes a promise he breaks it, and when he is entrusted with something he betrays the trust."
"3044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has three traits will find the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than everything else; that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; and that he hates returning to disbelief, after Allah has saved him from it, just as he would hate to be thrown into the Fire."
"3045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things bring destruction, three bring salvation, three are expiations, and three raise ranks. Those that bring destruction are: obeying greed, following one's desires, and a man's admiration of himself. Those that bring salvation are: being just in anger and in contentment, moderation in poverty and in affluence, and fear of Allah Almighty in private and in public. Those that are expiations are: waiting for the next prayer after a prayer, performing ablution thoroughly in the cold, and walking to the congregations. Those that raise ranks are: feeding others, spreading the greeting of peace, and praying at night while people are asleep."
"3046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are not refused as gifts: pillows, oil, and milk."
"3047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three things in which joking is not permissible: divorce, marriage, and freeing a slave."
"3048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are not withheld: water, pasture, and fire."
"3049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of three people is answered: the father, the traveller, and the oppressed."
"3050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom it is a right upon Allah Almighty to help: the one who strives (does jihad) in the path of Allah, the mukatab slave who wishes to pay off his amount, and the one who marries seeking chastity."
"3051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three people are under the guarantee of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: a man who goes out to one of the mosques of Allah, a man who goes out for jihad in the path of Allah, and a man who goes out for Hajj."
"3052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people upon whom Allah has made Paradise forbidden: the habitual drinker of wine, the one who is disobedient to his parents, and the cuckold (dayyuth) who tolerates indecency among his family."
"3053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people, all of whom Allah guarantees: a man who goes out for jihad in the path of Allah; Allah is his guarantor until He takes his life and admits him into Paradise, or returns him with reward or spoils. And a man who goes to the mosque; Allah is his guarantor until He takes his life and admits him into Paradise, or returns him with reward. And a man who enters his house with a greeting of peace (salam); Allah is his guarantor."
"3054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three practices of the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah) which people will not abandon: attacking people's lineage, wailing over the dead, and saying, 'We were given rain by such-and-such a star.'"
"3055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are from the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah): boasting about ancestry and lineage, attacking people's lineage, and wailing."
"3056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are part of good fortune and three things are part of misfortune. Of good fortune: a righteous wife who pleases you when you look at her, and whom you can trust with herself and your wealth when you are away from her; a riding animal that is smooth-paced so that it brings you up with your companions; and a house that is spacious with many amenities. And of misfortune: a wife who displeases you when you look at her and who hurts you with her tongue, and whom you cannot trust with herself and your wealth when you are away from her; a riding animal that is sluggish, such that if you beat it, it wears you out, and if you leave it, it does not bring you up with your companions; and a house that is cramped with few amenities."
"3057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of three people does not rise above their ears: the runaway slave until he returns, a woman who spends the night while her husband is displeased with her, and the imam whom the people dislike."
"3058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not ask about three people: a man who separated from the community (jama'ah), disobeyed his leader and died in a state of disobedience; a female or male slave who ran away from his master and died in that state; and a woman whose husband is absent, who has provided her with the needs of this world, yet after him she goes out adorned and displaying herself. Do not ask about them."
"3059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not ask about three people: a man who contends with Allah over His lower garment (izar), and a man who contends with Allah over His cloak (rida), for Allah's cloak is grandeur and His lower garment is might; and a man who is in doubt about the matter of Allah and in despair of Allah's mercy."
"3060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not come near three people: the drunkard, the one smeared with saffron, the menstruating woman, and the one in a state of major ritual impurity (junub)."
"3061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not come near three things: the corpse of a disbeliever, the one smeared with khaluq (a saffron-based perfume), and the one in a state of major ritual impurity (junub), unless he performs ablution (wudu)."
"3062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three people will never enter Paradise: the cuckold (dayyuth), the woman who adopts the manner of men, and the habitual drinker of wine."
"3063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three people will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the cuckold (dayyuth), and the woman who adopts the manner of men."
"3064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not reject the supplication of three people: the one who remembers Allah abundantly, the oppressed, and the just ruler."
"3065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""From three people Allah will accept on the Day of Resurrection neither an obligatory deed nor a voluntary one: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the one who reminds others of his favours, and the one who denies divine decree (qadar)."
"3066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah Almighty will neither speak to on the Day of Resurrection nor look at: a man who swore a false oath about his goods that he had been offered a price for them which he had not actually been offered; a man who swore a false oath after Asr in order to seize the wealth of a Muslim man by it; and a man who withheld his surplus water. Allah will say: 'Today I withhold My bounty from you, just as you withheld the surplus of that which your hands did not make.'"
"3067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah Almighty will neither speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at, nor purify, and for them is a painful punishment: the one who lets his lower garment hang below his ankles, the one who reminds others of his favours and never gives anything without reminding of it, and the one who sells his goods by means of false oaths."
"3068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah Almighty will neither speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at, nor purify, and for them is a painful punishment: a man who has surplus water in the wilderness and withholds it from the wayfarer; a man who sold goods to someone after Asr and swore by Allah that he had bought them for such-and-such, and the buyer believed him although the truth was otherwise; and a man who pledged allegiance to a ruler only for worldly gain: if he gives him some of it, he stays loyal, and if he does not give him, he does not stay loyal."
"3069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah Almighty will neither speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify, nor look at, and for them is a painful punishment: an old man who commits adultery, a lying ruler, and a proud poor man."
"3070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah will not look at tomorrow on the Day of Resurrection: an old man who commits adultery, a man who has made oaths his merchandise and swears over every matter, true or false, and an arrogant poor man who struts about."
"3071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the mannish woman who imitates men, and the cuckold (dayyuth). And three people will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of the favours he has given."
"3072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify, and for them is a painful punishment: an old man who commits adultery, a proud poor man, and a man who has made the name of Allah his merchandise: he does not buy except with an oath, and he does not sell except with an oath."
"3073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three people are given their reward twice: a man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then found the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and believed in him (peace and blessings be upon him) as well, followed him and affirmed him; he will have a double reward. And a slave who fulfilled the right of Allah and the right of his master; he will have a double reward. And a man who had a slave woman, raised her well, then taught her good manners well and educated her well, then freed her and married her; he will have a double reward."
"3074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people whom Allah loves and three people whom Allah hates. (Those He loves are:) a man who meets the enemy with a company and puts his chest before them until he is killed or wins victory for his companions; and a party who travel and their night journey grows long until they long to touch the ground, so they dismount, and one of them goes aside and keeps praying until he wakes them for their departure; and a man who has a neighbour who harms him, yet he bears his harm patiently until death or departure separates them. And those whom Allah hates are: the merchant who swears many oaths, the arrogant poor man who struts about, and the miser who reminds others of his favours."
"3075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three people supplicate to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, but they are not answered: a man who has a woman of bad character as his wife but does not divorce her; a man who is owed money by another man but did not have witnesses appointed over it; and a man who gave his wealth to a foolish person, even though Allah Almighty has said: 'And do not give the foolish your wealth.'"
"3076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The price of wine is unlawful, the earnings of a prostitute are unlawful, the price of a dog is unlawful, and the drum is unlawful. And if the owner of the dog comes to you seeking its price, fill his hands with dust. And wine and gambling are unlawful, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"3077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The price of a dog is impure, the earnings of a prostitute are impure, and the earnings of a cupper are impure."
"3078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On two occasions supplication is not rejected: supplication at the time of the call to prayer (adhan), and supplication at the time of rain."
"3079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On two occasions supplication is not rejected: supplication at the time of the call to prayer (adhan), and during battle when people are locked in combat with one another."
"3080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One third, and even one third is a lot."
"3081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One third, and even one third is a lot. Your giving charity from your wealth is charity, your spending on your family is charity, and what your wife eats from your wealth is also charity. And that you leave your family well off is better than leaving them stretching out their hands to people."
"3082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One third, and even one third is a lot. That you leave your heirs wealthy is better than leaving them needy, stretching out their hands to people. And whatever you spend seeking the pleasure of Allah, you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you put in your wife's mouth."
"3083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A previously married woman has more right over herself than her guardian, and a virgin should be asked permission by her father regarding her marriage, and her permission is her silence."
"3084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A previously married woman expresses her consent herself, and the consent of a virgin is her silence."
"3085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The married man and woman (who commit adultery) are to be both flogged and stoned, and the unmarried man and woman (who commit fornication) are to be flogged and exiled."
